"text":"A view of the matching rows, as of this moment."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each row is a tuple of the entity, labeled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entity"},{"type":"text","text":", followed by one value per term: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component for a component term, and a tuple of optionals for an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AnyOf","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" term. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"following example reads the name of every entity pushed by wind, thrust or both, with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forces it feels:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Name(value: \"kite\"), Wind(force: 3))","world.spawn(Name(value: \"rocket\"), Thrust(force: 5))","world.spawn(Name(value: \"rock\"))","","var forces: [String] = []","for (_, name, (wind, thrust)) in world.query(Query(Name.self, AnyOf<Wind, Thrust>.self)) {","    forces.append(\"\\(name.value): \\((wind?.force ?? 0) + (thrust?.force ?? 0))\")","}","print(forces)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"kite: 3.0\", \"rocket: 5.0\"]\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rock holds neither a wind nor a thrust, so it doesn’t match the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AnyOf","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" term."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The view is lazy: it finds the matching entities as you iterate it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"t","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"t","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{